    "# Topic Extraction & Stance Analysis: Pre-Processing, Dual-Track Extraction, and Codebook Architecture\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook provides a complete technical guide to the **Topic Extraction and Stance Analysis Pipeline** ([`T2 - Topic Extraction and Stance Analysis`](.)), detailing the end-to-end process through which raw congressional speaking turns are cleaned, attributed to legislators, segmented into indexed sentences, extracted via dual-track prompt architectures, consensus-clustered into a 111-topic policy codebook, and validated against external political science ground truth.\n",
    "\n",
    "--- \n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. End-to-End Workflow & Output Flowchart\n",
    "\n",
    "### Pipeline Flowchart\n",
    "\n",
    "```mermaid\n",
    "flowchart TD\n",
    "    subgraph S1 [\"Step 1: Roster Attribution & Turn Preparation\"]\n",
    "        A[\"Hearings Dataset<br/>(hearings_sst.parquet: ~116k turns)\"] --> B[\"Member BioGuide Attribution<br/>(speakers.py: anchored surname matching)\"]\n",
    "        B --> C[\"Cleaned Legislator Turns Stream\"]\n",
    "    end\n",
    "\n",
    "    subgraph S2 [\"Step 2: Sentence Segmentation & Windowing\"]\n",
    "        C --> D[\"pysbd v0.3.4 Segmenter (stance.py)<br/>Paragraph-by-paragraph segmentation\"]\n",
    "        D --> E[\"clean_turn_sentences<br/>Drop adjournment appendices, label echoes, stage directions\"]\n",
    "        E --> F[\"Windowing (40 sentences/block)<br/>Globally numbered: [1] .. [N]\"]\n",
    "    end\n",
    "\n",
    "    subgraph S3 [\"Step 3: Dual-Track Extraction Passes\"]\n",
    "        F --> G1[\"Track 1: Hearing-Level Summary Topics<br/>(TRACK1_USER -> Ranked top-5 neutral noun phrases)\"]\n",
    "        F --> G2[\"Track 2: Member-Level Stance Records<br/>(USER -> [sentences, topic, stance: support|concern])\"]\n",
    "        G2 --> H[\"merge_adjacent_records & parse_records<br/>Directional linting (lint_topic)\"]\n",
    "    end\n",
    "\n",
    "    subgraph S4 [\"Step 4: Consensus Clustering & Codebook Freezing\"]\n",
    "        G1 --> I[\"Pooled Phrase Embeddings (BGE-large)<br/>HDBSCAN + LLM Consensus Clustering\"]\n",
    "        H --> I\n",
    "        I --> J[\"Frozen 111-Topic Policy Codebook<br/>(frozen_codebook_111.parquet)\"]\n",
    "    end\n",
    "\n",
    "    subgraph S5 [\"Step 5: Panel Assembly & Longitudinal Stance\"]\n",
    "        J --> K[\"Map Stance Records to Codebook Topics\"]\n",
    "        K --> L[\"member_stance_panel.parquet<br/>(Congress, Member BioGuide, Topic, Stance, Evidence)\"]\n",
    "    end\n",
    "\n",
    "    subgraph S6 [\"Step 6: Benchmark Evaluation & Quality Audit\"]\n",
    "        L --> M[\"CAP Crosswalk Alignment (T2.3.1)<br/>184 Policy Subtopics (92.4% rank pct)\"]\n",
    "        M --> N[\"Quality Audit & Figures (T2.3.2)<br/>Polarization networks & attention curves\"]\n",
    "    end\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Pipeline Stages and Output Matrix\n",
    "\n",
    "| Stage | Module / Script | Primary Operations | Input Data | Generated Output Artifact & Type |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| **1. Attribution & Ingestion** | `speakers.py` & `T2.1.1` | Matches member surnames to BioGuide IDs using committee rosters (>99.8% precision). | Raw GovInfo transcripts (`hearings_sst.parquet`) | **Attributed Turns Table** (`list[dict]` with `bioguide_id`, `speaker_name`, `text`) |\n",
    "| **2. Segmentation & Filtering** | `stance.py` (`clean_turn_sentences`) | Pinned `pysbd` (v0.3.4) sentence splitting; strips adjournment appendices, echoes, and stage cues; 40-sentence windows. | Attributed Turns | **Indexed Sentence Blocks** (`list[dict]`: `block_idx`, `sentences`, `start_idx`) |\n",
    "| **3. Track 1 Extraction** | `stance.py` (`render_track1`) | Extracts 2–5 ranked neutral topic noun phrases per hearing summary to capture overall attention. | Hearing Summaries (`T1`) | **Summary Topic Lists** (`list[dict]`: `rank`, `topic`, `topic_lint`) |\n",
    "| **4. Track 2 Extraction** | `stance.py` (`render_user`) | Extracts index-cited stance records: sentence indices, neutral noun phrase topic, and binary stance (`support` / `concern`). | Indexed Sentence Blocks | **Stance Records JSON** (`list[dict]`: `sentences`, `topic`, `stance`, `topic_lint`) |\n",
    "| **5. Post-Parse Validation** | `stance.py` (`merge_adjacent_records`) | Validates consecutive indices ($\le 3$), lints directional words, merges contiguous same-topic records. | Stance Records | **Validated Stance Records** (`interim/stance_records/`) |\n",
    "| **6. Codebook Freezing** | `T2.2.2` | Consensus clusters pooled phrases into 111 canonical policy topics with frozen definitions. | Pooled Track 1 & Track 2 phrases | **`frozen_codebook_111.parquet`** (111 topic taxonomy) |\n",
    "| **7. Panel Assembly** | `T2.2.2` | Maps records to codebook topics, creating longitudinal member-hearing stance panel. | Validated Records + Codebook | **`member_stance_panel.parquet`** (`cleaned/02_topic_extraction/`) |\n",
    "| **8. Quality Evaluation** | `T2.3.1` & `T2.3.2` | Crosswalks topics to Comparative Agendas Project (CAP) ground truth; generates polarization figures. | Stance Panel + CAP Codebook | **`cap_alignment.parquet`** + **`polarization_network.pdf`** |"
   ]
  },
