    "--- \n",
    "\n",
    "## 2. Document Pre-Processing, Turn Attribution, and Sentence Indexing\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1. Speaker Attribution via Committee Rosters (`speakers.py`)\n",
    "- Uses official congressional BioGuide committee rosters to disambiguate identical surnames (e.g. \"Mr. Smith\").\n",
    "- Applies anchored surname heuristics, achieving **>99.8% precision** across ~116,000 member turns.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2. Sentence Segmentation & Cleaning (`stance.py`)\n",
    "- **Pinned Segmenter**: Uses `pysbd` (v0.3.4) applied paragraph-by-paragraph to prevent quote-mark runaway segmentation.\n",
    "- **Deterministic Cleaning Rules (`clean_turn_sentences`)**:\n",
    "  1. *Truncation at Adjournment*: Strips post-adjournment submitted statements and written Q&A (`[Whereupon the hearing adjourned]`).\n",
    "  2. *Inserted Statements*: Truncates at `[The prepared statement of X follows:]`.\n",
    "  3. *Speaker Label Echo Removal*: Drops leading name echoes (e.g. `\"Senator Dorgan.\"`).\n",
    "  4. *Stage Directions & Headers*: Drops `\"[Laughter.]\"`, `\"[Applause.]\"`, and all-caps inline headings.\n",
    "- **Global Index Numbering & Windowing**:\n",
    "  - Formats sentences into globally numbered blocks: `[1] Sentence one\\n[2] Sentence two`.\n",
    "  - Long turns (>40 sentences) are partitioned into 40-sentence windows with continuous numbering (`windows(sentences, size=40)`)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Demonstrating Sentence Segmentation, Cleaning, and Numbering from T2.X/stance.py\n",
    "import re\n",
    "\n",
    "sample_turn_text = \"\"\"Senator Nelson. Thank you Mr. Chairman. [Applause.]\n",
    "NASA's commercial crew program has demonstrated remarkable launch reliability.\n",
    "However, we must address the persistent budget delays facing deep space communications infrastructure.\n",
    "[The prepared statement of Senator Nelson follows:]\n",
    "Additional inserted written testimony...\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Truncation regex matching\n",
    "_TRUNCATE_AT = re.compile(r\"\\[\\s*Whereupon|hearing (?:was |is )?adjourned|\\[The [^\\]]{0,80}follows[:.\\]]\", re.IGNORECASE)\n",
    "_STAGE_DIRECTION = re.compile(r\"\\[[^\\]]{2,60}\\]\\.?\")\n",
    "\n",
    "raw_sentences = [s.strip() for s in sample_turn_text.split(\"\\n\") if s.strip()]\n",
    "kept_sentences = []\n",
    "for s in raw_sentences:\n",
    "    if _TRUNCATE_AT.search(s):\n",
    "        break\n",
    "    if _STAGE_DIRECTION.fullmatch(s) or s.startswith(\"Senator Nelson.\"):\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "    kept_sentences.append(s)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"--- Numbered Sentences for Prompt Injection ---\")\n",
    "for i, s in enumerate(kept_sentences, 1):\n",
    "    print(f\"[{i}] {s}\")\n"
   ]
  },
